[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "48094108-5cf9-57df-96d7-24531e1c14fc",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+2y &=8 \\\\ 2x+y &=-2 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=-2 \\\\ -y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n2x+(-14)=-2\\,\u27f9\\,x=6.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ebecc690-c29e-5c35-9259-bc9a37f55c87",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
