  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "68e36f78-5e20-5c0d-aec6-b63636e4cf25",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y &=-5 \\\\ 4x+16y &=-10 \\\\ -6x-24y &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & -10 \\\\ -6 & -24 & 15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & -10 \\\\ -6 & -24 & 15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -24 & 15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ffcd1ebd-464e-5e0a-baf4-ae28c1a98e1e",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
